      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Though the documentation says nothing, not only Gravity, we can't change PhysBone properties by animation at run-time. Maybe it's a kind of optimizations for processing speed.\nThis is also not described in the doc but, after changing properties by animations, you can let PhysBone re-read properties by altering Enabled property of PhysBone component . (change Enabled to false and change again to true)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "6261d444dd670b5721f5eeab",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5f317eed9dcbb575795c3c32",
        "alias": "Silver Wildfowl",
        "aliasID": "65e2621da6e3ea79ddec7d5c",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/8f6fd3075d61793186f1cd503e0c21cd.png",
        "created": "2020-08-10T17:07:57.568Z",
        "name": "eru",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "61ae60302a0c8153e557fd42",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2022-04-21T22:01:40.600Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "62251ac3e182580d016ccfde",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 5
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For visual record:\nhttps://streamable.com/as70t2\nAs you can see, when changing GestureLeftWeight, Gravity property of physbone is changing accordingly, but doesn't update on scene. It does update after re-enabling whole component, which in my case causes visually bad snapping and completely removes fluidity when raising ears. It would be great to see physbones behaving the same way as dynamic bones in this scenario.\nMy suggestion would be to add some kind of another \"isAnimated\" toggle/checkbox to every property so we can select which we are going to animate. Or add possibility to animate properties too when \"IsAnimated\" is true (the one about bone transforms).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
